# The dispatch line in the executable is sh and JavaScript at once, and only
# one arrangement of it is both. Prettier reads it as JavaScript and writes
# `':'; //;` — still valid JavaScript, no longer valid sh, because `:` loses its
# argument and the shell tries to *run* `//`. Every command then prints
# "//: is a directory" to stderr before working. `pnpm format` is a documented
# script, so without this line any contributor who runs it ships that.
